WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.962
Every camp, every clinic around America I go and talk to kids, 

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:06.506
they don't ask, like, "Man, how did it feel to play 19 years? 

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.383
How did it feel to play with Dirk or win a—"

00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:10.385
- Win a championship, yeah. What question they ask?

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:12.846
- How did it feel for LeBron to dunk on you like that?

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.388
- [Laughing]

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:14.347
- Like, c’mon man. Get outta here.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:22.897
♪♪♪ 

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.402
- New year, new season of Untold Stories,
and we're listening to what the fans want.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:31.322
We started off with football. Now we're
branching off across different sports. 

00:00:31.322 --> 00:00:32.699
So who we got in the pool hall today? 

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:35.577
- Hey!
- Oh, we got the Jet on the runway. 

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:36.619
- Yes, sir.

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:37.537
- Jason Terry, what's good with you, baby?

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.496
- Man, all is well!

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.540
- This is one of my favorite
episodes we about to do,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.876
cuz this is talking about
my favorite team in the world: 

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.044
the Dallas Mavericks, man. 

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.087
And you've had some great memories on that team, man. 

00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:48.590
We gonna get into that. But I gotta see how nice you are on this table, man.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.424
- Oh yeah, 

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:50.508
oh yeah.
- Go ahead and break it, man.

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:52.719
- C’mon, man. I got a little bit of something.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.056
Drop, ball!

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:58.266
- Going into 2011, 

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:00.685
what was the confidence level that you had?

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:02.103
And what was the confidence level the team had?

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.730
- You already know, though.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.858
The ultimate, ultimate, ultimate prediction, right?

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:10.653
Not the week before the game, or the day of the game.

00:01:10.653 --> 00:01:12.405
Like, this is in preseason.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.241
In training camp, we're at DeShawn Stevenson's house. 

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.910
We're having some team bonding. 

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.245
And we walk in, man, and he's like, 

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.331
"Man, I got a tattoo artist. Man, he gonna come through.

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:23.750
You know, y'all get whatever you want. It's on me." 

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.001
Like, "Oh, OK. Cool." 

00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:27.962
Me, I'm a man of many tattoos. All of 'em have meaning.

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:30.465
But this time I was like, "Man, I'm about to do something." 

00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:34.260
And so I get the Larry O'Brien Trophy tatted on my bicep,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.804
but I didn't reveal it that night.

00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:36.763
Wrapped it up, went home. 

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.890
Then at shootaround the next day, we're in Orlando, 

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.060
Coach Carlisle, "Bring it in, everybody. OK, let's get ready to roll tonight."

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.187
I'm like, "Hold up, fellas. I got something for you." 

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:45.355
And I unwrapped it.

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:46.147
Boom. 

00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:47.315
And then I flexed, 

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:49.234
but it was like crickets. Like, everybody was looking around like—

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:51.361
- [Laughing]
- What?

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:52.737
And Dirk just bust out,

00:01:52.737 --> 00:01:55.115
"This guy is crazy.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:55.657
- [Laughing]

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:58.118
He's a circus. Look at this guy."

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:01.830
I'm like, "Nah, man, I'm serious. I think we got the team that's gonna do it."

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.289
And then we went on our journey.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.792
Uh oh. 

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.502
Got a pool shark in the building.

00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:08.128
- [Laughing]

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.213
I know, I know what time it is now.

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:12.757
- Game 6, I was an ESPN Dallas intern 

00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:15.760
watching the fanwatch that was going on in American Airlines Center

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:16.928
while y'all was in Miami.

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:20.098
Seconds count down. You see Dirk hopping off the floor. 

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:25.478
Every team is doing this now, where you see them going to Vegas, going to 
a big club after they win a championship to celebrate. 

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.898
Y'all was the first ones really keeping this thing lit on social media. 

00:02:28.898 --> 00:02:32.986
I was geeked. I didn't know what to do. I couldn't go to sleep, 
and I was 20, so I couldn't go out to bars. 

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.195
You know, I didn't have a fake ID.

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:39.325
- That was the biggest celebration ever in the history because you did it in their city. 

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:44.873
The owner is with you striking up the band, like, you don't see that. 
You don't see owners, like, really just out there. 

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:49.669
But to walk through their prestigious Club LIV, with the trophy, one, 

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.006
and then this big ass wheelbarrow of ice.

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.258
To this day I haven't seen a bottle of Champagne that big. 

00:02:55.258 --> 00:02:58.219
And it was probably at least three-quarters of this pool table. 

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:01.097
- Reportedly, that tab was 110,000 dollars.

00:03:01.097 --> 00:03:01.764
- Wow.

00:03:01.764 --> 00:03:03.141
- What do you remember from that night, man? 

00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:04.517
Cuz I'm mad I wasn't there.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.519
- Man, I remember Lil Wayne

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.479
definitely gave us a shoutout on the mic.

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:10.899
I remember Cuban get on the stage with the mic.

00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:12.609
Dirk was on stage with the mic.

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:13.818
After that, it's a blur.

00:03:13.818 --> 00:03:14.986
- Let's get a shot in real quick.

00:03:14.986 --> 00:03:15.570
- Yup.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.615
- You’re there for another year with the Mavs.

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:19.032
- Yup.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:19.991
- Try to do this repeat. 

00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:20.992
Doesn't work out.

00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:21.993
From there you go to Boston. 

00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:22.869
- Mmhmm.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:23.870
- Same level of confidence?

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.121
- Aw, man.

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:26.956
Now I'm an NBA champion.

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:27.582
- [Laughing]

00:03:27.582 --> 00:03:30.293
I'm about to go join some other champions.

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:33.296
Growing up it was Celtics-Lakers. That was the rivalry. You watched it. Like, 

00:03:33.296 --> 00:03:34.756
that was our social media.

00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:36.507
You wanted to see what those two were gonna do.

00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:38.426
Now I get to join that franchise,

00:03:38.426 --> 00:03:39.719
and for me it's like, man.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.970
We got a real shot.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.847
Miami was still running things in the East.

00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:43.556
- 100 percent.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.433
- I was there one year, but I will tell you this.

00:03:45.433 --> 00:03:47.936
Boston got some of the greatest sports fans ever,

00:03:47.936 --> 00:03:50.772
and every time I go back, it's all love.

00:03:50.772 --> 00:03:51.356
- For real?

00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:54.484
- Like, you would think I won a championship and played there, like, my whole career.

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:56.486
- You think it's off the strength of that tattoo? What do you think it's from?

00:03:56.486 --> 00:03:58.988
- It couldn't have been how awful how LeBron did me.

00:03:58.988 --> 00:04:00.240
- [Laughing]
Right? 

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.574
- And how he, how he meme-ified me.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:04.869
- Talk to me. What do you remember about that play? 
What do you remember about that moment?

00:04:04.869 --> 00:04:09.582
- I wanna say it's one of the lowest moments in my career, but at the same time,

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.084
I mean, I'll forever go down in history. 

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.294
Like, you got dunked on by The King.

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:13.711
- [Laughing]

00:04:13.711 --> 00:04:17.799
- Every camp, every clinic around America I go and talk to kids,

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:19.217
they don't ask, like,

00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:23.054
"Man, how did it feel to play 19 years? How did it feel to play with Dirk or win a—"

00:04:23.054 --> 00:04:24.430
- Win a championship, yeah.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.598
What question they ask?

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.726
- How did it feel for LeBron to dunk on you like that?

00:04:28.726 --> 00:04:30.103
- Like, c’mon man. Get outta here. 

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:31.312
- What was it, a fast break?

00:04:31.312 --> 00:04:34.399
- Yup. It was a fast break. But what happened was, I was coming down.

00:04:34.399 --> 00:04:35.900
I turned the ball over.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.317
- OK.

00:04:36.317 --> 00:04:39.779
- So it's just instinct for me when you turn it over, “I got to get it back.” 

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.907
So I'm chasing it. I mean, I might've chased their whole team and the coach

00:04:42.907 --> 00:04:43.950
trying to get the ball back.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:47.120
I got Chalmers coming at me, and then LeBron's coming down the middle. 

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.372
I took my eye off of LeBron for one second,

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:50.999
chased Chalmers,

00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:54.627
turned back around, and he was already in the air, like—

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:55.336
- [Laughing]

00:04:55.336 --> 00:04:57.046
- in slow motion,

00:04:57.046 --> 00:05:00.383
and what made me jump is what I'm trying to figure out.

00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:01.175
- [Laughing]

00:05:01.175 --> 00:05:02.176
- Like, there's no reason—

00:05:02.176 --> 00:05:04.262
like, even if you did jump—

00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:06.014
- You not gonna touch that, man.

00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:07.849
- You ain't touching that.

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:09.350
No. 

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.935
And I jumped, man.

00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:12.812
He lifted me on his knee,

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.647
and I was still going up with him.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.524
Like, LeBron just bang, bang, it was over.

00:05:16.524 --> 00:05:18.818
Like, I elevated. I was in the rim.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.611
- [Laughing]
And hit the ground, man.

00:05:20.611 --> 00:05:23.156
I didn't hop up quick. I laid there for a minute.

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:25.533
And I think that's the picture, the meme, that's out. 

00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:27.285
Like, I'm laying there with my arms folded.

00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:27.994
- [Laughing]

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.454
- Like being in a funeral, man.

00:05:29.454 --> 00:05:34.125
- I can't front, bro. I was one of those people on 
social media just dying laughing at this moment.

00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:36.919
- For three weeks, I was checking my phone

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:38.671
and people were sending me messages like, “Man, you OK?”

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:42.050
Like, numbers I haven't heard in, in eight years,

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:45.053
I'm seeing numbers pop up. “Jet, are you good?”

00:05:45.053 --> 00:05:46.763
“You dead, big homie? You good?”

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.431
I'm like, “I don't know what these people talking about.”

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:50.516
They even said on Wikipedia, they said

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.601
that was my death date.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.269
It had the date and everything on there. 

00:05:53.269 --> 00:05:54.604
That's crazy, man.

00:05:54.604 --> 00:05:57.190
- The internet don't give a damn about nobody, bro.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.608
It is undefeated.
- Undefeated.

00:05:58.608 --> 00:05:59.567
- What was the response from your teammates?

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.402
- Oh, they was killing me in the locker room,

00:06:01.402 --> 00:06:02.195
destroying me.

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.780
Jokes and jokes and jokes.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.406
I'm telling you, it kept up for a while.

00:06:06.991 --> 00:06:07.658
All right.

00:06:12.747 --> 00:06:14.665
- Jason Terry, you got 60 seconds.

00:06:14.665 --> 00:06:17.460
See how many shots you can get in, but also let’s see 
how many questions you can answer. You ready?

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.836
- Man, this is what I do.

00:06:18.836 --> 00:06:21.172
- All right, let’s get it, man. Let’s start this thing off right.

00:06:21.172 --> 00:06:24.217
In three, two, one, let’s get it!

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.968
- More fun playing with, Dirk or KG?

00:06:26.427 --> 00:06:27.678
- KG.

00:06:27.678 --> 00:06:29.972
- Jet, do you prefer private jets or commercial, man?

00:06:29.972 --> 00:06:31.182
- Private.

00:06:31.182 --> 00:06:32.600
- Celtics or Mavs? Don’t let me down!

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.768
- C’mon, Mavs.

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:34.644
- Let’s go, baby!

00:06:34.644 --> 00:06:36.270
Luka or Giannis?

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.980
- Like Drake said, both.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:38.856
- [Laughing]

00:06:38.856 --> 00:06:40.608
Biggest memory of the Warriors Mav series?

00:06:40.608 --> 00:06:44.654
- Man, when Dirk threw the chair and put a hole in the stadium.

00:06:44.654 --> 00:06:46.489
Best three-point shooter in NBA history?

00:06:46.489 --> 00:06:47.990
- Steph Curry.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:49.867
- Best trash-talker you’ve ever played with?

00:06:49.867 --> 00:06:51.536
- Kevin Garnett.

00:06:51.536 --> 00:06:53.371
- Who did more for the headband, you or LeBron?

00:06:53.371 --> 00:06:54.872
- Oh, yours truly.

00:06:54.872 --> 00:06:57.125
- Who's the real Jet, you or Kenny Smith?

00:06:57.125 --> 00:06:59.752
- The Jet by name, and not by game.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:00.837
- I’m sorry, Kenny Smith.

00:07:00.837 --> 00:07:02.630
Best city you’ve ever visited on the road?

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.423
- Seattle.

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.090
- Seattle!

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.508
- All-Star Weekend or Super Bowl Weekend?

00:07:05.508 --> 00:07:06.551
- All-Star.

00:07:06.551 --> 00:07:07.760
- MJ or LeBron?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.761
- MJ!

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.304
- Funniest teammate you’ve ever had?

00:07:10.805 --> 00:07:12.306
- Greg Buckner.

00:07:12.306 --> 00:07:14.434
- Loudest locker room guy you’ve ever played with?

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.393
- Corey Brewer.

00:07:15.393 --> 00:07:17.728
- Eight seconds! Pregame snack routine that you've ever had?

00:07:17.728 --> 00:07:18.521
- Chicken fingers.

00:07:18.521 --> 00:07:20.481
- Who are you listening to before a game, man?

00:07:20.481 --> 00:07:22.650
- Man, Nipsey Hussle the great.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.319
- And that’s time right there. 28 scores.

00:07:25.319 --> 00:07:27.238
We gonna end this on “The Marathon Continues.”

00:07:27.238 --> 00:07:27.655
Jet—

00:07:27.655 --> 00:07:29.824
- Man, appreciate you.
- appreciate you pulling up to the pool hall with us, man.

00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:30.366
- Love.

00:07:33.369 --> 00:07:36.122
- Subscribe to Bleacher Report for
more Untold Stories.

